  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Assignment to Clingendael to review and provide input for Netherlands-funded Private Sector Development initiatives in Chad</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Embassy Office of the Netherlands in Chad, in close collaboration with RVO, commissions an assignment to review and provide input for the Dutch Private Sector Development (PSD) strategy in Chad, including Dutch-funded initiatives aimed at PSD in Chad. 

The input will draw on a deep understanding of the political economy context in Chad and contain practical advice that can inform an update of the existing PSD strategy for Chad. To this end, the advice will also take into account the position of the Netherlands in Chad and uncertainties and limitations regarding future Dutch funding for development cooperation.
 
Advice should be linked to new policy themes &#x201c;Dutch interests&#x201d;, stability and security, migration, and aid for trade, which are expected to be the focus in a new policy letter expected early 2025, and any other policy changes that may be announced throughout the course of this assignment.</narrative>
  </description>
